   "src/elspeth/contracts/declaration_contracts.py:implements_dispatch_site": "FunctionDef(name='implements_dispatch_site', args=arguments(args=[arg(arg='site_name', annotation=Name(id='DispatchSiteName', ctx=Load()))]), body=[Expr(value=Constant(value='Mark a method as implementing a named dispatch site.\\n\\n    Two purposes (H2 \u00a7Acceptance AST-detectability + D1 correction):\\n\\n    1. Runtime: ``register_declaration_contract`` inspects class methods for\\n       this marker to build the per-site registration map. Methods without\\n       the marker are NOT invoked by the dispatcher for any site, even if\\n       their name happens to match a ``DispatchSite`` value.\\n    2. Static: ``manifest.contract_manifest`` ``elspeth-lints`` MC3a/b/c rules\\n       AST-detect the decorator on concrete contract classes. Required for\\n       multi-level-inheritance detection per the D1 correction on H2\\n       (``subclass.__dict__`` does not see mixin-inherited overrides).\\n\\n    Validates ``site_name`` at decoration time against the DispatchSite enum.\\n    A typo raises ``ValueError`` at module import rather than silently\\n    mis-registering.\\n\\n    Per the defensive-programming prohibition\\n    (docs/guides/data-trust-and-error-handling.md \u00a7The Defensive Programming\\n    Prohibition): direct membership check on the frozen set of valid values.\\n    No ``getattr`` default, no silent pass-through.\\n    ')), If(test=Compare(left=Name(id='site_name', ctx=Load()), ops=[NotIn()], comparators=[Name(id='_DISPATCH_SITE_VALUES', ctx=Load())]), body=[Raise(exc=Call(func=Name(id='ValueError', ctx=Load()), args=[JoinedStr(values=[Constant(value='@implements_dispatch_site('), FormattedValue(value=Name(id='site_name', ctx=Load()), conversion=114), Constant(value=') \u2014 unknown dispatch site. Must be one of '), FormattedValue(value=Call(func=Name(id='sorted', ctx=Load()), args=[Name(id='_DISPATCH_SITE_VALUES', ctx=Load())]), conversion=114), Constant(value='.')])]